    "objects": {
      "general": [
        {
          "properties": {
            "paragraphs": [
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "What this suggests",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "13pt",
                      "fontWeight": "bold"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "1. The SMS lift grows with age: about +1.4 pp for under-25s (CI includes 0) and +1.6 pp for 25-34, rising to +5.9 pp for 65+ (CI +4.8 to +7.0).",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "12pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "2. This is not the spend effect in disguise: median spend is similar across age bands, and the youngest clients spend the least yet respond the least.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "12pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "3. Age and spend stack: among clients in the two lower spend quartiles, 65+ gain about +7.8 pp; among higher-spend clients aged 25-34 the lift is under +1 pp (matrix).",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "12pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "4. Gender matters less: women +4.0 pp vs men +2.9 pp and not-stated +2.9 pp; the female and male intervals overlap.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "12pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "5. Implication: older, lower-spend clients respond most to the SMS; young and high-spend clients barely respond.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "12pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "drillFilterOtherVisuals": true
  }
}